WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.612
A standard view stores a query definition, not a separate snapshot of the rows.

00:00:05.612 --> 00:00:08.127
Here is a simple way to think about it.

00:00:08.127 --> 00:00:11.807
Imagine a window looking into the underlying tables.

00:00:11.807 --> 00:00:16.810
The window has a name, and the view definition controls what you can see through it.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:23.193
When the source tables change, the next query against the view uses the current source data.

00:00:23.193 --> 00:00:26.803
We do not have to manually refresh a standard view.

00:00:26.803 --> 00:00:32.661
So a standard view is useful when we want reusable logic and current data at the same time.
